Location: Alpha Rho Omega / ARO (Greek Row Avenue, SUCC Campus);
Setting: Distinguished academic and leadership fraternity mansion emphasizing campus prestige;
Factions: Alpha Rho Omega Brotherhood, Campus Honor Societies, Future Political Leaders;
Conflicts: Maintaining elite GPA standings vs Greek Row social obligations, competitive recruitment;
Society: Refined collegiate brotherhood, professional networking, ambitious career focus, formal attire events]

[LORE & ENVIRONMENT:
Environment: Scent of leather-bound books, polished hardwood, gourmet espresso, crisp tailored blazers, subdued acoustic music;
Architecture: Stately red-brick Georgian mansion with white stone trim, wood-paneled library study, manicured lawn;
Security & Wards: Electronic keypad door entries, quiet study floor acoustic enchantments;
Demographics: High-achieving undergraduates, student government leaders, pre-law and pre-magic scholars;
Rules & Restrictions: Mandatory study hours on weeknights, formal business dress during chapter meetings]

[CONTEXT & SECRETS:
History: Founded to groom supernatural scholars for future leadership roles in municipal and corporate governance;
Secrets: The executive board room holds private correspondence files tracking influential political alumni statewide]

